  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 953 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nBy Thursday morning, a strong cold front will have passed southeast\nthrough the TN Valley, with blustery north winds developing. \nLingering showers in the strong cold advection aloft will persist in \nour northeast counties. Elsewhere, a stratus or stratocu deck will \npersist, limiting much solar heating to counter the cold advection. \nSo temperatures will likely remain steady in the 50s much of the day.\nWind gusts of 25-30 mph are likely through much of the day. \nOvernight lows will then dip into the lower to middle 30s.\n\nA large gyre will remain in place over the Great Lakes region through\nFriday, then shift east over the weekend. This will maintain a steady\nand deep layer northerly flow across much of the eastern CONUS. A\nwidespread freeze has a high probability of occurrence Friday and\nSaturday nights with lows in the middle to upper 20s for most areas.\nHighs will only be in the lower 50s Saturday in valley areas and\nmiddle to upper 40s atop the Cumberland Plateau. Highs recover into\nthe upper 50s to lower 60s on Sunday.",
